      "Language": "dut",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 18-year-old woman experienced abnormal and painful vaginal tissue loss while using an oral contraceptive. A pregnancy test was negative. Histopathological examination of the tissue showed a decidualised endometrium. We made the diagnosis of progesterone-induced membranous dysmenorrhoea."},
